<title>NETHERLANDS: Aalberts buys German firm.</title>
<headline>Aalberts buys German firm.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch industrial holding Aalberts NV said on Wednesday it was in talks about the takeover of German Seppelfricke ArmaturenGroep, with a turnover of about 100 million marks.  </p>
<p>Aalberts said the takeover would be partly paid with its own recources and partly with the new shares.</p>
<p>The new shares will be brought into the market by ABN AMRO Hoare Govett.</p>
<p>&quot;The takeover will contribute to the growth in earnings per share,&quot; the firm said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
